# PAM configuration file for Cyrus Murder mupdate service.
#
# This file configures the PAM (Pluggable Authentication Modules) stack for
# the Cyrus Murder (mupdate) daemon. It dictates how authentication and
# account validation are handled for Cyrus users.
#
# If you want to use Cyrus in a setup where users don't have
# accounts on the local machine, you'll need to make sure
# you use something like pam_permit for account checking.
#
# Remember that SASL (and therefore Cyrus) accesses PAM
# modules through saslauthd, and that SASL can only deal with
# plaintext passwords if PAM is used.
#

# PAM include directive for authentication.
# This file is included to determine how user credentials are verified
# (e.g., password checking, LDAP lookups, etc.).
# Default: common-auth
@include {{ common_auth_include | default('common-auth') }}

# PAM include directive for account management.
# This file is included to determine if the user's account is valid,
# expired, or has other restrictions (e.g., login times, shell restrictions).
# Default: common-account
@include {{ common_account_include | default('common-account') }}